# The [[platform]] land-ride bench (30960): two floors that DO NOT touch. The west "ground" is at height 0;
# the east "deck" is 200 up. A walkmesh vertex y is the engine's own frame, where up is NEGATIVE (the kit's
# selfY = -worldY convention: `land = [x, z, 200]` rides to selfY -200), so the deck's verts sit at y = -200.
# A 400-unit gap (x -200..200) with no triangles and no links: the ONLY way onto the deck is the ride.
# Footprint matches the walkmesh-sensor bench (x -1220..1220, z -1931..257), so its camera frames it.
v -1220 0 257
v -200 0 257
v -200 0 -837
v -1220 0 -837
v -200 0 -1931
v -1220 0 -1931
v 200 -200 257
v 1220 -200 257
v 1220 -200 -837
v 200 -200 -837
v 1220 -200 -1931
v 200 -200 -1931
o ground
f 1 2 3 4
f 4 3 5 6
o deck
f 7 8 9 10
f 10 9 11 12
